#1
&nA Cleared Trail &+gThrough The Jungle&N~
   &nA gradual trail, roughly fifty paces wide, of cleared
&+gforest floor meanders southward through the jungle. Thick
&nbrush, including exotic flowers, tall shadowy trees, and
&+glush vines twist and thrive in this temperate terrain.
&nA light mist fills the wooded floor while the air is full
&+gof the chirping, howling, and hooting of the native wild-
&Nlife. Further north, the trail narrows and tends to branch
&+goff into the wild. Southward, conversely, the trees begin
&nto thin and the distant sound of crashing waves is heard.
~
1 33554432 3
D2
~
~
0 0 2
