#2
&+gA Jungle &nClearing &nof &+yCrow's Cages&N~
   &+gThe jungle has been cleared at this intersection of
&+gtrails, converging at a ring of several old, rusted metal
&+ycrow's cages. A wide, cleared trail through the jungle
&+yextends to the north, while a trail through a darkening
&+gjungle opens to the east, and a descending trail towards
&+gthe shore to the west. Roughly twelve large, rusty cages
&+ysit in a large ring around the center of the clearing,
&+yfacing inward. Such a place was likely used as a prison
&+gfor banished rogues and vagabonds that were imprisoned
&+gto make an example of such types. Beyond the clearing,
&+yand swallowing the jungle trails, the jungle grows thick.
~
