#4
&+LDeep Within the &+gForbidden Forest of the Khomani-Khan&n~
&+g  The forest gorged the light, a thick canopy of gnarled, twisting
&+Gbranches casting merging shadows that blanket the moss-covered
&+gfloor. The air is foggy, heavy with a taste of decaying vegetation
&+Gand a scent of earthy musk, fresh rain, and the sounds of life.
&+gInsects and birds constantly buzz and chirp, filling the humid air
&+Gwith an ongoing melody. The dark forest seems to breathe and sing
&+gat once, an ancient composition that has obvious attractions to the
&+GKhomani-Khan, lored cat-people and keepers of this place.
~
