#29
&nA Foggy, Still Lake Deep Within the Jungle&N~
   The natural depression in the earth here has formed a drainage
spot where rainwater irrigates after particularly inclement weather.
A thick, everpresent fog settles across the entirety of the shallow
lake, which itself is only two-to-three feet at its deepest. The
jungle is ripe with vegetation, with thick brambles and thorny
thickets seemingly everywhere. The fog gradually wisps into the
air like the smoke from freshly-burned incense, although it is
much less odoriferous. The thick jungle continues across a gentle
slope that curls around the lip of the lake before evening out into
the thick, green melange. Despite the lake's seclusion, it is
anything but 'still' as flies, waterbugs, and occasional critters
create constant ripples and small splashes across the waters, leaving
it fully undisturbed only during small breaks.
~
