&+yThe Towering Wooden Gates of &+rM&+La&+rn&+Ls&+rh&+La&+rk&+La&N~
   &+yA wide, unpaved road leads way northwards towards a valley of
&Nrock formations, while to the south lies the great walls of the
&+yport city Manshaka, fabled home of the legendary portmaster Dalvik.
&nThe walls of the city are made of tightly-bound beams of straight
&+ytimber, cut a towering height and sharpened to massive points.
&nThe gates themselves are made of similar cut and carved timber,
&+yattached to a massive wheel that opens and closes across a huge
&ngravelly rut. Huge blocked stone pillars support the wooden joinsts,
&+ywhich also act as a perimeter guard's walk above.
~
