#173
Spectator Rows &+rBefore a Blood-Red Minaret&N~
&+r   The rows of wooden-planked spectator seats taper off along the
&+Rwestern face of the Blood Arena, giving way to a relatively short,
&+rslender stone voyeur tower. The tower is bloodstained with a deep
&+Rred, presumably from the excessive melee of constant gladiator
&+rduels, below. The minaret tower is accessed through a singular
&+Rwooden duel, almost too narrow for many of the common beasts in
&+rthe area - which suggests this may have been originally built by
&+Rothers, long ago.
~
