#200
&+gA Lobby Lounge of &+YThe Broken Mast~
   This large, rectangular inn sits on the boardwalk of Manshaka,
offering convenient lodging to seafarers and shoremen alike. The
framework of The Broken Mast is made of blocked stone, with heavy
timber joists supporting a spacious second floor, presumably used
for lodging. A large hearth sits at the center of this lobby,
above which bulbs of smoke find their way into a narrowing chimney.
Further north is a reception area, along with a winding staircase
that twists upwards to the bedrooms.
~
