#204
&+LThe Smoke-Filled &+yBarroom&+L of The Black Lotus~
   &+LDespite the grand stature of the building from the outside,
&+LThe Black Lotus truly seems at its largest when viewed from
&+Lthe interior barroom. Large stained oak benches and tables
&+Lsurround a central staircase, flanked on its corners by four
&+Lhuge stone pillars that dominate from floor-to-ceiling.
   &+LWide, well-made sofas line the spaces between two huge
&+Lbars, one on the north face and one on the west, that
&+Lmeet at a built-out corner space where dozens of massive
&+Lkegs are seemingly continuously carried in and out by the
&+Lhulking (and grinning) minotaurs that serve this establishment.
   &+LThe stone staircase leads up towards a guarded loft, where
&+Lthe mysterious leaders of the Black Lotus can best observe
&+Lits visitors, and down below to a second barroom where the
&+Lsmartest visitors might conceal their shadiest dealings.
~
