#205
&+LA &NSmokey &+YH&+Re&+rar&+Rt&+Yh&+R Room&+L of the &+WFrothy &+YCis&+ytern&N~
&+L   The large stone structure known locally as the Frothy Cistern has
&+Llarge rounded hearth chamber on it's southern face, casually spilling
&+Lan everpresent haze of smoke through the ports of the south-facing
&+Lsoffits onto Drudach street, below. The hearth is fed and maintained
&+Lby what seems to be a large family of local humans that bare common
&+Lsimilarities including angular faces and dark skin. A staircase of
&+Ldark, glossy-treated wood curls above the northern side of the hearth
&+Lchamber until it merges the joists of the second floor, above. The
&+Lblocked stone walls and floor meet at a central, circular firepit,
&+Labove which smoke is directed out of the south and eastern ports.
&+LThis structure's south-facing circular, slotted wall suggests it may
&+Lhave been formerly used as an archery's nest, overlooking the bay.
~
