&+MOdd&+Ci&+Mt&+mi&+Ce&+ms&N &+Land &+YCom&+Wmo&+Yd&+Witi&+Ye&+Ws&N~
   &+CThis makeshift boardwalk merchant stall is filled with all manners
&+mof relics, foreign weapons, seemingly magical items, potions, and exotic
&+Cor strange-looking foods. The stall itself appears to be large square
&+mtent made up of several layers of patched tarps, supported by various
&+Cpoles, planks, and shelves of varying origins. A ramshackle 'design'
&+mthat has been so roughly, yet frequently, maintained through the years
&+Cthat the structure has effectively melded with the boardwalk, similar
&+mto an in insect's nest.
&+C   A huge twelve-foot table divides the tent down the center, filled
&+mon both ends with huge shelves full of various boxes and small chests.
&+CA gap at the center serves as a window, through which business is
&+mconducted between the patrons and the proprietors. Larger and more
&+Cexotic items can be seen through the window and between gaps in the
&+mshelving, including imported exotic weapons, magical statues and totems,
&+Ctokens of wizardry including magical tomes and staffs, and anything
&+mof covetible value that the shopkeepers might profit from that it's
&+Cprevious owner might want to depart with quickly and conveniently.
~
