#207
&+yIn a Massive Log &+LWarehouse~
&+y   Massive logs of cured cypress and pine stacked into walls,
overlapping at the corners, form this enormous storage hold.
&+yLarge enough to be fit for a moderately-proserpous king,
this massive hold is arranged with large partitions of stacked
&+ylog walls into a few dozen storage areas. Each hold is stocked
with various goods including piled ship-building materials,
&+ypiles and sacks of rare earths, stacks of coiled cordage,
and even huge rolls of colorful imported textiles used for
&+ysails of the world's biggest battlecruisers.
   Dock hands and ship builders work in a constant flow in and
&+yout of the warehouse under the watchful eye of the strongest
guards Manshaka has.  All around the area the sounds of sawing,
&+ychopping, grinding, and yelling are heard as planks are planed,
masks are cut, moorings are fastened, and ship frames are pounded
&+yout. This large warehouse extends in a large east-west shape,
shading the tent stalls and smaller shops below.
~
