#218
&+LUnder A Stone Bridge &+bOn The River Olung&N~
   &+LThe river levels out and swiftly flows beneath the huge, blocked-
&+Lstone bridge above. One single support pillar reinforces the keystones
&+Lat the center of the bridge, forming a brief fork in the flow of the
&+LOlung. Even during the heaviest rains, the bridge has withheld for
&+Lmany years, despite heavy travel. Large matching banks of weeds and
&+Lsmall trees spring out from either side of the bridge, as the jungle
&+Lto the east thins to the eventual shore to the southwest.
~
