#242
&+CA Crystal Clear, Cold Mountain Lake Above the Clouds~
   &+CThis beautiful, crystal clear lake is the result of snow melt and
&+Cstorm rain runoff, collecting from the highest points in this rocky
&+Cmountain basin. At its point of least disturbance, this mountain
&+Cspring water flows with an inviting freshness and nourishment.
&+CSmooth, round pebbles of gray and dull red fill the basin, softly
&+Ceroded over time by the gentle weathering of this remote place.
&+CClouds hang low at one's eyeline, where the wind flows with the same
&+Cunimpeded pureness of the water. Several small streams branch off
&+Cfrom the water basin, gently crashing to other collection points
&+Camongst the mountain, below, eventually gathering in the River Olung.
~
