#259
&+yInside a Creaky &+WSaw&nmill&N~
   &+LThis old sawmill is made of huge planked hardwood, similar to
&+Lthe same material that it produces. A team of operators guide
&+Llong, debranched logs from the northern side of this open mill
&+Linto a sharp, toothed metal saw-blade attached to the arm on a
&+Lrotating hub, using rotational force generated by the waterwheel.
&+LOn the other side of the blade, a team of 'pullers' pull the
&+Lplaned wood freely and stack them accordingly.
   &+LThe sawmill only has partial walls on the western face, opposite
&+Lthe waterwheel, with large, open windows overlooking the freshly-
&+Ldeforested ridge line.
