#264
&NA Heavily-Trafficked Clearing&N~
   The forest in the ravine between Manshaka's port and Mount Olung
further east has proven to be a valuable and permanent source of
shipbuilding timber for the denizens of the docks, as evidenced by
this heavily-trafficked clearing beside a sizable hydro-powered
sawmill. Huge stacks of hardwood planks and bins of saws, axes,
heavy whetstones, and makeshift tents housing all of these tools
seem to line the entire southern and northern rocky faces. Deep
ruts dug into the mud from many years of large-wheeled vessels
traversing this intersection have permanently scarred the earth.
A twenty-foot wide logging trail passes from the south and west,
while the north has a large rocky ledge followed by a steep cliff.
The remains of an ill-maintained cobblestone path leads east into
the opening of an old wooden sawmill beside a massive waterwheel,
powered by the constant power of the River Olung.
~
