   &+LA gradual rocky slope angles eastward, eventually meeting the
softly-churning waters of a secluded whirlpool below a bifurcated
&+Lwaterfall. An earthen relief reaches up to the south into the
recently-harvested forested hillside beneath Manshaka. To the
&+Lnorth, mountainous juts escalate into the nearly-vertical base
of the natural mountain that the river divides. The westward slope
&+Lgrows with verticality, eventually over the treeline and the river,
ending at the eastern walls of Manshaka, from which the songs
&+Lfrom the many taverns seem to accompany the everpresent smoke from
their chimneys.
