#284
&+LA Smokey &+gGambling Den&N~
   &+LThis underground, hearthless chamber is heated only by the
&+gmassive bodies that typically occupy it.  Constructed massively
&+Lwith the same blocked stone and extra-thick wooden joists, one
&+gmight assume The Black Lotus has stood for as long as Manshaka.
&+LTwo large tapestries adorn the north and southern walls, while
&+gwest wall holds a single shelf, high up by the ceiling, dusty
&+Lwith a few identical steins and scattered bones. A rectangular
&+gtable, high from the ground but sturdy with patchwork reinforce-
&+Lments, sits at the center of six large wooden chairs in below-
&+gaverage condition.
~
1 33554432 0
D1
~
~
0 0 283
S
#285
&+rA Feasting Hall&N~
   &+rThis cavernous cellar, perhaps as an area to brew the spirits
&+Lserved at The Black Lotus, has been renovated into a feasting
&+rhall for the highest caste patrons. A massive table, easily able
&+Lto fit eighty men, or twenty minoutaurs, was assembled at the
&+rcenter of the chamber, lined with hearty quad-footed stools.
&+LSlaves of smaller races can be found skittering about, between
&+rtheir harrowing horned lords, constantly struggling to keep them
&+Lsated. A strangely-guarded closet is situated at the far south-
&+rwestern corner of this feasting hall.
~
1 33554432 0
D2
