#312
&+yA R&ni&+yck&Ne&+yty &+YLight&+chouse &+yDock&N~
   &+yLong planks of battered wood that have been replaced
&+yagain and again make up this rickety dock, large enough
&+yfor a medium ship at best. Two large posts on either
&+yside of the dock support the end, extending roughly
&+yfifteen meters into the bay.  A rusty anchor, tied taut
&+yto the inner post, slowly erodes in the salty surf.
&+yTo the north, a blocked-stone lighthouse, older than
&+ythe port itself, greets those nearing Manshaka.
~
