#322
&+yA Rutted &+gLogging Road&N~
&+y   This well-travelled forest road is cut in straight paths through the
otherwise unforgiving valley that neighbors the port city Manshaka.
&+yDirectly south, past a steep drop-off, the vast ocean dominates the
horizon, dotted with distant cargo and fleet ships from all corners
&+yof the realms. The ground here is rutted from frequent trips dragging
timber down the ridgeline, above, towards the sawmill, below. The
&+yrecently-cut parts of the forest still have younger trees and saplings
standing, robbed only of the thicker, stronger, mature timber.
~
1 33554432 3
D1
~
~
