#469
&+cA Lower Foyer of &+BThe Trade Guild&N~
   &+cThis blocked-stone foyer has a high, two-story ceiling and
&+Lis overlooked by a railed balcony above, flanked by twin stair-
&+ccases that access the upper levels. Wide, gradual stone steps
&+Llead downward from the eastern wall into a smoke-filled office
&+cfrenzied of the bustle of heavy trade deals in Manshaka. The
&+Lhuge double-doors leading into The Trade Guild are made of fine,
&+cheavy moorwood and are almost always open, closing only during
&+LManshaka emergencies.
~
