#472
&+WThe Temple of Poseidon&N~
   &+WThis open-aired temple of pillared stone stands upon a
&+Wcarved-out ledge that overlooks the bay of Manshaka. Several
&+Wlong steps lead down towards the western end of the temple,
&+Wwhere a huge statue of Poseidon presides over a gaping hole
&+Win the center of the floor, where waves crash rhythmically,
&+Wsending misty bursts of salty seaspray into the temple in
&+Wa constant-soaking. Strange coral, barnacle, and seaweed
&+Wgrowths decorate the walls, adopting this place like a reef.
~
1 33685504 0
D1
~
~
0 0 157
